Defining scope and objectives: what is in the project and what is explicitly out.
Feasibility study: technical, economic, operational, legal, and schedule feasibility, ending in a go/no-go decision.
Estimation: effort, cost, and duration (person-months, budget, timeline).
Scheduling: breaking work into tasks, sequencing them, and setting milestones.
Resource planning: team roles, skills, hardware, software, tools, and budget.
Risk planning: identify, analyse, and prepare responses to risks.
Quality planning: standards, review points, and testing strategy.
Communication and configuration planning: reporting, meetings, version control, change control.
